sk Force on Alzheimer's Disease</article-title><source>Neurology</source><year>1984</year><volume>34</volume><fpage>939</fpage><lpage>944</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6610841</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Huppert</surname><given-names>FA</given-names></name><name><surname>Brayne</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Gill</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Paykel</surname><given-names>ES</given-names></name><name><surname>Beardsall</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>CAMCOG- A concise neuropsychological test to assist dementia diagnosis: socio-demographic determinants in an elderly population sample</article-title><source>Br J Clin Psychol</source><year>1995</year><volume>34</volume><fpage>529</fpage><lpage>541</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8563660</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Athey</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Walker</surname><given-names>RW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Demonstration of cognitive decline in Parkinson's disease using the Cambridge Cognitive Assessment (Revised) (CAMCOG-R)</article-title><source>Int J Geriatr Psychiatry</source><year>2006</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>977</fpage><lpage>982</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16955442</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/gps.1595</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chodosh</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Petitti</surname><given-names>DB</given-names></name><name><surname>Elliott</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Hays</surname><given-names>RB</given-names></name><name><surname>Crooks</surname><given-names>VC</given-names><